# The two views GENERATED from the bug ledger in docs/bugs/.
#
# NOT tracked, and that is load-bearing rather than tidy. Every code PR is
# required to add an entry, so a committed copy of either view is rewritten by
# every PR and therefore conflicts on every PAIR of concurrent PRs — by
# construction, not by carelessness. That is the same failure the single-file
# BUG-HISTORY.md had, and re-tracking these would import it straight back.
#
# `audit:bug-index` and `audit:bug-history` regenerate them in memory and gate
# on the GENERATOR working (parse failure, unresolvable area tag, zero entries),
# which never needed a copy in git. Read them locally with
# `npm --prefix backend run gen:bug-index` / `gen:bug-history`.
docs/generated/bug-index.md
docs/generated/bug-history.md

# The extracted AutoCount line photographs (export-ac-line-photos.py) and the
# resume sidecars beside them. Thousands of JPEGs whose home is R2, not git —
# and a half-finished export must never look like a reviewable diff.
# The MANIFESTS at the top of that directory are deliberately NOT ignored: they
# are the snapshot the attach scripts read, and swapping one in is a reviewed
# commit (the same rule export-ac-reimport.py's snapshots follow).
backend/scripts/data/line-photos/*/

# Python bytecode from the backend/scripts/*.py exporters. The runbook now tells
# people to run those, and nobody should be able to commit a .pyc by accident.
backend/scripts/__pycache__/
